[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2176468394","pull_request_review_id":2973563769,"id":2176468394,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6BukWq","diff_hunk":"@@ -783,7 +783,7 @@ void AnimationLibraryEditor::update_tree() {\n \t\t\tfor (const uint64_t &lib_id : collapsed_lib_ids) {\n \t\t\t\tObject *lib_obj = ObjectDB::get_instance(ObjectID(lib_id));\n \t\t\t\tAnimationLibrary *cur_lib = Object::cast_to<AnimationLibrary>(lib_obj);\n-\t\t\t\tStringName M = mixer->get_animation_library_name(cur_lib);\n+\t\t\t\tStringName M = cur_lib == nullptr ? StringName(TTR(\"[Global]\")) : mixer->get_animation_library_name(cur_lib);","path":"editor/plugins/animation_library_editor.cpp","commit_id":"a87b096d3ba9336a87666a3766f77f70ea863df4","original_commit_id":"12524534149decdf6834ebb0d7c9ffde5c1b6282","user":{"login":"lyuma","id":39946030,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5OTQ2MDMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39946030?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma","html_url":"https://github.com/lyuma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The only place `\"[Global]\"` is used in the code, is the suffix of the tree item. It is never used as a StringName.\r\n```cpp\r\n\tfor (const StringName &K : libs) {\r\n\t\tTreeItem *libitem = tree->create_item(root);\r\n\t\tlibitem->set_text(0, K);\r\n\t\tif (K == StringName()) {\r\n\t\t\tlibitem->set_suffix(0, TTR(\"[Global]\"));\r\n\t\t} else {\r\n\t\t\tlibitem->set_suffix(0, \"\");\r\n\t\t}\r\n```\r\nAs we can see in this code snippet, in the case that a global library is used, the element `K` in `libs` is `StringName()` in this case, not `StringName(TTR(\"[Global]\"))`\r\n\r\nHowever, it makes sense that we don't want error spam, and we also don't want it to match the name of an existing animation library (unless the user names their library `[Global]`). So would it be better to continue in the null case?\r\n```suggestion\r\n\t\t\t\tif (cur_lib == nullptr) {\r\n\t\t\t\t\tcontinue;\r\n\t\t\t\t}\r\n\t\t\t\tStringName M = mixer->get_animation_library_name(cur_lib);\r\n```","created_at":"2025-07-01T05:36:30Z","updated_at":"2025-07-01T05:37:17Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107430#discussion_r2176468394","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107430","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2176468394"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107430#discussion_r2176468394"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107430"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2176468394/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":786,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":5,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2178061016","pull_request_review_id":2976184203,"id":2178061016,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6B0pLY","diff_hunk":"@@ -783,7 +783,7 @@ void AnimationLibraryEditor::update_tree() {\n \t\t\tfor (const uint64_t &lib_id : collapsed_lib_ids) {\n \t\t\t\tObject *lib_obj = ObjectDB::get_instance(